# (1.4.0) PRESET spun fast: a piece's chord slots stay its own. The engine takes a piece over a few blocks and
# publishes its slots as it goes; the UI took them into whichever piece it was on by then, so a piece passed through
# kept the last one's (the Winter Set's Snowfield held Aurora's GM7). Chamber's first four written (Fm, Gm, Am, Bbm),
# then PRESET spun 0 -> 4 -> 0 at 5, 10 and 20 ms a click: Basic keeps its walk, Chamber its four
listen
wait 3000
expect piece 0
turn PRESET 1 300
wait 800
expect piece 1
tap EDIT
wait 400
expect view 15
spin K2 -100
wait 200
tapkey 0
wait 200
turn K1 1
wait 200
spin K2 -100
wait 200
tapkey 2
wait 200
turn K1 1
wait 200
spin K2 -100
wait 200
tapkey 4
wait 200
turn K1 1
wait 200
spin K2 -100
wait 200
tapkey 5
wait 200
expect par72 2
expect par73 2
expect par74 2
expect par75 2
tap HOME
wait 300
turn PRESET -1 300
wait 800
expect piece 0
expect par72 0
expect par73 0
turn PRESET 4 5
wait 800
turn PRESET -4 5
wait 800
turn PRESET 4 10
wait 800
turn PRESET -4 10
wait 800
turn PRESET 4 20
wait 800
turn PRESET -4 20
wait 800
expect piece 0
expect par72 0
expect par73 0
expect par74 0
expect par75 0
turn PRESET 1 300
wait 800
expect piece 1
expect par64 5
expect par72 2
expect par73 2
expect par74 2
expect par75 2
turn PRESET 1 300
wait 800
expect piece 2
expect par72 0
expect par73 0
